    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Practical cookery</span> allows students to apply theoretical knowledge of meat, poultry, milk, sea foods, and additives to real dish preparation. This topic focuses on planning, preparing, cooking, and serving dishes safely and attractively using these protein foods and additives.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Planning a Practical Session</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Good practical work begins with planning: choosing a suitable recipe, listing ingredients and quantities, preparing a time plan (order of tasks matched to cooking times), and gathering equipment before starting.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Hygiene and Safety in Practical Work</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Before cooking: wash hands, tie back hair, wear an apron, and ensure the work surface and equipment are clean. During cooking: avoid cross-contamination between raw meat/poultry/fish and ready-to-eat foods by using separate boards and utensils, and cook protein foods to a safe internal temperature.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Combining Foods and Additives in a Dish</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">A well-planned dish (e.g., a stew combining meat, fish, and seasoning additives) should balance flavour, colour, and texture. Herbs and spices are added at appropriate cooking stages — some early for depth of flavour (e.g., ginger, garlic), others late to preserve aroma (e.g., fresh herbs).</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Serving and Presentation</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Dishes should be served promptly after cooking, at the correct temperature, attractively garnished, and portioned appropriately. Presentation affects the overall appeal and perceived quality of a meal.</p>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> A common practical assessment criterion is avoiding cross-contamination — always use separate chopping boards/utensils for raw meat, poultry, and fish versus foods that will be eaten without further cooking.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Practical cookery combines planning, hygiene, correct use of additives, and attractive presentation to produce safe, nutritious dishes from meat, poultry, milk, sea foods, and food additives.\n</div>\n",
