    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Energy management</span> in food preparation means organising kitchen tasks and using time, effort, and resources wisely to reduce fatigue and improve efficiency. It helps the cook complete meal preparation with minimal stress and waste.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning of Energy Management</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Energy management refers to the planned, efficient use of human energy (effort) and physical resources (time, fuel, equipment) during food preparation to avoid unnecessary fatigue and wastage.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Advantages of Energy Management</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Good energy management reduces tiredness and stress, saves time, prevents wastage of fuel and ingredients, improves the quality and timing of meals, and allows the cook to accomplish more tasks with less effort.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Principles of Energy Management</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Principle</th><th>Explanation</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Planning ahead</td><td>Organise tasks and gather materials before starting</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Good posture and working height</td><td>Work surfaces at a comfortable height reduce strain</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Grouping tasks</td><td>Combine similar tasks (e.g., all chopping together) to save movement</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Using the right tools</td><td>Correct equipment for the task saves time and effort</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Minimising unnecessary movement</td><td>Arrange the kitchen so frequently used items are within reach</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Rest periods</td><td>Take short breaks to avoid fatigue during long preparation</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Meaning of Fatigue</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Fatigue is a state of physical or mental tiredness resulting from prolonged effort, poor working conditions, or inefficient work methods. In the kitchen, fatigue can be reduced by proper planning, good posture, correct equipment, and organised movement.</p>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> WAEC often asks for \"steps in managing energy\" — remember: plan ahead, group similar tasks, use correct tools/equipment, maintain good posture/working height, minimise movement, and take rest breaks.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Energy management involves planning, organising, and using effort efficiently in food preparation to reduce fatigue, save time and resources, and improve meal quality.\n</div>\n",
