    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Kitchen equipment and utensils</span> are the tools used to prepare, cook, and serve food. Knowing how to classify, select, use, and care for them properly ensures efficient, safe, and long-lasting kitchen work.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning and Classification</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Kitchen equipment includes all tools, appliances, and fixtures used in food preparation. They are classified by size and function:</p>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Classification</th><th>Examples</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Large equipment</td><td>Cooker/stove, refrigerator, oven, sink</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Small equipment/utensils</td><td>Pots, pans, knives, spoons, bowls, sieves</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Fixtures</td><td>Built-in cabinets, worktops, shelves</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Appliances</td><td>Blender, mixer, toaster, kettle</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Selection of Kitchen Equipment</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">When selecting equipment, consider: the material (stainless steel, aluminium, non-stick coating), durability, ease of cleaning, size of family/kitchen, cost, and safety features.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Use of Kitchen Equipment</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Each tool should be used strictly for its intended purpose — e.g., a chopping board for cutting, a sieve for straining — to avoid damage, inefficiency, or safety hazards.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Care and Storage</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Equipment should be washed and dried properly after use, sharp tools stored safely (e.g., knives in a block or sheath), and items stored in a way that prevents damage, rust, or contamination. Regular maintenance (e.g., sharpening knives, checking appliance cords) extends equipment life.</p>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> WAEC commonly asks students to classify kitchen tools as large or small equipment, and to state factors considered when selecting equipment (durability, cost, ease of cleaning, safety, material).\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Kitchen equipment is classified as large equipment, small utensils, fixtures, or appliances. Selection depends on material, durability, cost and safety, while proper use, care, and storage extend their lifespan.\n</div>\n",
