    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Labour saving devices</span> are tools and appliances designed to reduce the time, effort, and physical labour needed to complete kitchen and household tasks, making food preparation faster and less tiring.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning of Labour Saving Devices</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">A labour saving device is any tool or appliance — manual or electrical — that reduces the amount of physical effort and time required to perform a kitchen task compared to doing it entirely by hand.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Examples of Labour Saving Devices</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Device</th><th>Task Made Easier</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Blender/food processor</td><td>Grinding, blending, pureeing</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Electric mixer</td><td>Whisking, beating, kneading</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Pressure cooker</td><td>Faster cooking of tough foods (beans, meat)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Microwave oven</td><td>Quick reheating and cooking</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Dishwasher</td><td>Washing dishes</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Grater/peeler</td><td>Faster grating/peeling than a knife</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Uses of Labour Saving Devices</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">These devices reduce fatigue, save time, increase precision and consistency in food preparation, and allow the cook to handle larger quantities of food more easily than manual methods.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Factors to Consider in Selecting Labour Saving Devices</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Consider: cost, durability, ease of use and cleaning, power supply requirements, safety features, size relative to kitchen space, and the specific needs of the household.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">5. Care and Maintenance</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Labour saving devices, especially electrical ones, should be used according to manufacturer instructions, cleaned after use, kept away from water when not designed to be submerged, and checked periodically for damaged cords or parts.</p>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> WAEC often asks students to list labour saving devices and match them to the specific task they simplify — e.g., blender for grinding/blending, pressure cooker for fast cooking of tough foods.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Labour saving devices (blenders, mixers, pressure cookers, microwaves, etc.) reduce time and physical effort in food preparation. Selection should consider cost, safety, ease of use, and household needs, with proper care extending their usefulness.\n</div>\n",
